    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Help, we have a major crisis. One of our refrigerated containers for a shipment of fresh tuna just lost power mid-transit. The temp readings jumped from -18C to 4C in under an hour. I need a checklist of immediate steps to handle the immediate spoilage risk and what I need to do regarding safety protocols for the remaining stock.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To address the crisis, immediately:\n\n* Isolate the refrigerated container immediately by setting it to \"isolation\" mode to prevent further cross-contamination.\n* Assess the temperature and take note of the time and conditions of the temperature jump to determine the extent of the damage.\n* Confirm hold time procedures, if applicable, and fulfill them as recommended.\n* Monitor and evacuate the space for any tainted tuna.\n\nFor the remaining stock, ensure that:\n\n* Temperature control is closely monitored, and all necessary steps are taken to maintain it within the safe range.\n* HACCP procedures are followed, including chlorination and puncturing or proper disposal of compromised tuna.\n* Necessary documentation is maintained, including any incident reports and communication with regulatory authorities.\n\nPrioritize the well-being and safety of people consuming the tuna and take swift action to address the situation.",
